Subject: [PATCH] docs(rules): settle the self-hosted font licence (D10 §13 Q2)

Q2 is answered: free open-licence faces only, no foundry licence is bought.
Both rule files still say the face list "awaits"/"is pending" that decision,
which is now stale, and the conditional wording in build-rules ("until it is
taken") no longer has a condition to wait on.

The replacement states the rule positively and keeps the reason attached: a
per-domain or pageview-capped licence disqualifies a face, because the
pipeline ships one site per client across unlimited domains and nobody
reviews a licence per run. The Turkish glyph check is unchanged — it was
never a licence question.

Both files are hook-protected, so this is an operator apply:

    git apply docs/patches/A5/01-font-licence.patch

Decision recorded in docs/D10-design-variation.md §13 and docs/DECISIONS.md
D10 (amends D4).

